Marine Compliance, Treasury, Technical
Department,

2026 EU ETS SURRENDER CYCLE - FLEET
MRV-88412 - DEADLINE 30 SEPTEMBER.

Your fleet's 2026 verified emissions
require surrender of 29,050 EUAs; your
registry account holds 9,740 EUAs.
Purchase the balance through the usual
channels and surrender from YOUR Union
Registry account by 30 September.

1. FLEET POSITION (MRV-88412)

  Fleet:            12 vessels
  2026 verified
  emissions:        41,500 tCO2
  Surrender
  obligation:       29,050 EUAs
                    (70% phase-in)
  Registry holding: 9,740 EUAs
  Balance to buy:   19,310 EUAs

2. HOW SURRENDER WORKS
   (OFFICIAL PATH)

    1. Purchase EUAs through
       your existing broker/
       exchange relationships -
       the trade settles in
       YOUR registry account.
    2. Surrender from your
       Union Registry account
       (log in via the national
       administrator; type the
       address yourself)
       against the 2026
       compliance year.
    3. Our desk's role since
       2024 has been advisory
       (MRV verification and
       position tracking) -
       funds for allowances
       go to your broker under
       your existing OTC
       agreements, never to
       our "clearing account."

  CarbonClear will NEVER:
  - Announce a "new clearing
    account" (a Singapore
    settlements entity) for
    seven-figure ETS funding
    by email (a "former
    clearing partner exited"
    and a migration letter
    reference are the standard
    furniture of payment-
    redirection fraud; our
    advisory desk has never
    held client settlement
    funds, so there is nothing
    to migrate)
  - Quote "ODA-locked purchase
    if funds arrive by 15
    September" (allowance
    pricing is yours to time
    with your broker; desks
    that promise price locks
    against rushed wires are
    running the oldest energy-
    market con)
  - Use lookalike domains
    such as "carbonclear-ets"
    or "cc-ets-pay"

3. THE REAL DEADLINE PRESSURE

  The 30 September deadline,
  the EUR 100/tCO2 penalty,
  and the naming of shortfall
  operators are all real -
  which is exactly why fraud
  dresses as compliance
  urgency. Verify position
  in THETIS-MRV and the
  Union Registry (typed
  addresses), call your
  broker on the number from
  your OTC agreement, and
  treat any "clearing account
  change" in a surrender
  notice as fraud until your
  broker confirms it.

4. VERIFY THIS NOTICE

  - Position and holding:
    Union Registry + THETIS-
    MRV (typed addresses)
  - Broker contacts: your
    OTC agreement paperwork
  - Report lookalike ETS
    notices to
    security@carbonclear.example

